\chapter*{Preface}
\addcontentsline{toc}{chapter}{Preface}
This book follows an On1x program from source to executable. The early
chapters teach the language and its value and resource models. Later
parts walk through projects, the compiler and its backends, and the
boundary between an On1x program and a MuLIB kernel or native host.

Command examples begin at the MuLIB repository root unless a different
working directory is given. Listings taken from repository examples may
be excerpts. A heading called Repository sources links to manuals,
implementation, or tests in the source snapshot on which the chapter
is based. The revision is \texttt{2cdceb9c}. Use those links to resolve
details that depend on the selected build, target, or ABI. The book
calls out bounded and optional profiles where they affect a reader's
choice of syntax, backend, build tool, or library.

